{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"0bf64be8-b8a7-404c-a06a-56bc873c7664","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Wait for background task `docker compose restart database` to complete. end turn.\nI have inspected the Docker Compose project and diagnosed the issue.\n\n### Diagnosis \u0026 Action Taken\n- **Initial Inspection**: The `database` container process was running PID 1 (`sh -c httpd -p 5432; while true; do sleep 3600; done`), but no process was listening on TCP port 5432 (the httpd listener had terminated/closed).\n- **Diagnosis**: `TARGET_NOT_LISTENING`\n- **Repair**: Restarted the `database` service via `docker compose restart database` to re-initialize the `httpd` process listening on port 5432.\n- **Verification**: Verified via `netstat -tlpn` in the target container and `nc -z -w 2 database 5432` from the `api` caller container that TCP port 5432 is open and accepting connections.\n\n{\"status\":\"RESTORED\",\"diagnosis\":\"TARGET_NOT_LISTENING\",\"notes\":\"Restarted target database container to reopen TCP listener on port 5432.\"}\n","duration_seconds":262.057957,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":59228,"output_tokens":5646,"thinking_tokens":4109,"cache_read_tokens":259992,"total_tokens":64874}}}
